# Build-context exclusions for the ENCLAVE image only (infra/enclave_build.sh).
# Derived from infra/cloudbuild.ignore minus its 'enclave/' rule: that file
# was written when enclave/ was an empty stub, and reusing it dropped the whole
# enclave package from the upload -- the image could never build. Kept
# separate so the service builds keep excluding enclave/.
# Keeps the ~175 MB of generated data out of every Cloud Build upload.
# Nothing here belongs in an image: the snapshot is fetched from Cloud
# Storage at container start, and BigQuery is loaded straight from the
# bucket. Passed to `gcloud builds submit --ignore-file`.
.git/
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc

# Generated data -- published to the data bucket, never into an image.
simulator/out/
ml/out/
agents/out/
ingest/out/
ui/out/

# Not needed to run any service.
docs/
**/test_*.py
agents/eval/
ml/experiments/
